{"kind": "tool_approval", "tool": "book_chapter_save_draft", "args": {"body": "The air in the archives was thick with the scent of old parchment and something sharper, like the ozone before a lightning strike. Elara traced the embossed sigil on the cover of the Ember Codex, her fingers trembling. It wasn't just the weight of the book that unsettled her, but the warmth radiating from the leather—a steady, rhythmic pulse that felt far too much like a heartbeat.

She had spent years searching for this relic, following whispers through the shadowed corners of the Great Library, but seeing it now, under the dim light of the mage-lamps, felt less like a discovery and more like a confrontation. The legends had always said the Codex was a vessel, but they had never mentioned it was alive.

As she whispered the opening incantation, the sigil flared with a dull, crimson light. The shadows in the room didn't just retreat; they seemed to recoil, as if the light itself were a physical weight pressing against the darkness.", "book_id": "01a05c99-572c-74a3-9061-ce55fded0214", "chapter": "Chapter I — The Ember Codex", "chapter_id": "01a05c99-57e8-7bf0-9748-48d108f36195"}, "tier": "A"}

